Exploratory Data Analysis on Iris Dataset
Project Overview

This project performs Exploratory Data Analysis (EDA) on the Iris flower dataset using Python.

Objectives
Understand the dataset and its features.
Calculate descriptive statistics.
Check for missing values and duplicate records.
Visualize species distributions and measurement patterns.
Analyze correlations between numerical features.
Tools and Libraries
Python
Pandas
Matplotlib
Seaborn
Scikit-learn
Methodology
Load the Iris dataset.
Inspect the data and calculate summary statistics.
Check data quality.
Create visualizations using bar charts, boxplots, scatter plots, and a correlation heatmap.
Interpret the findings.
Key Findings

The dataset contains three Iris species with 50 records per species. Petal measurements help distinguish between species, and the visualizations reveal relationships between flower measurements.

Conclusion

This project demonstrates how exploratory data analysis and data visualization can help identify patterns and understand a dataset.

How to Run

Open iris_eda.ipynb in Google Colab and run the cells in order.
